<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex says cut jobs 2.1 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex says cut jobs 2.1 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state oil and gas monopoly cut jobs by 2.1 percent in 1996 compared with the previous year, the company said in a presentation of its 1996 results.</p>
<p>Pemex employed a total 128,591 people at the end of 1996, compared with 131,392 employees at the close of 1995.</p>
<p>Fewer people were employed in each of the company's divisions, except for in Pemex's Exploration and Production unit, which accounted for most of 1996 profits.</p>
<p>Pemex's Refining division, the only unit to lose money in 1996, saw a 6.3 percent drop in employees for the year.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
